`document.getElementById('touch-btn-fire')` is null, and querySelector is also returning null. In other words, the combat cluster isn't being rendered at all. Why? The `withCombat` helper passes `regime: 'space'` plus the combat props. `renderControls` spreads `props` with default values:

```tsx
function renderControls(props: Partial<Parameters<typeof TouchControls>[0]> = {}): HTMLDivElement {
  ...
  root.render(
    <TouchControls
      enabled={props.enabled ?? true}
      regime={props.regime ?? 'space'}
      source={props.source ?? source}
    />,
  );
```

The helper only passes `enabled`, `regime`, and `source`! The combat props (`onFire` etc.) are not being forwarded. Need to update `renderControls` to forward arbitrary props. Let's fix the helper so it can spread additional props.

